                  <div class="sisf-m-content sisf-content-grid"><h1 class="sisf-m-title text-white entry-title">Our Team</h1></div></div></div></div></div><main><section class="ag-sec"><div class="container"><h2>Meet our team</h2><p>Our people are the strength of Arowolo Group: a highly skilled, purpose-driven workforce backed by a wide network of OEM partners, delivering safe, reliable and cost-effective energy solutions.</p><div class="row gy-4 mt-3"><div class="col-sm-6 col-lg-3"><div class="ag-member"><div class="ph"><img src="images/team/bintu-fatimoh-ajanaku.jpeg" alt="Ajanaku Bintu Fatimoh" style="object-position:top"></div><h3>Ajanaku Bintu Fatimoh</h3><span> Director</span><p style="height: 270px;overflow: auto;">Bintu Fatimoh Ajanaku, who holds a 33% stake in the company, is a visionary leader whose influence is particularly strong in the oil and gas industry. With deep expertise in global energy markets, she played a crucial role in the company’s successful entry into this competitive field. Bintu’s strategic thinking has been key in forming important partnerships and advocating for sustainability, helping the company establish itself as a leader in the sector. She  champions  innovation,  particularly  through  supporting  advanced technologies that improve operational efficiency in drilling and exploration. Additionally, Bintu is committed to incorporating renewable energy into traditional oil and gas operations, ensuring the company thrives now and remains sustainable in the future.
A dedicated advocate for women in the energy industry, she actively works to create  leadership  opportunities  for  women  in  the  traditionally  male- dominated sector. Bintu’s global influence extends to negotiating exploration agreements with multinational corporations, unlocking valuable oil reserves across the world. As a director, she continues to guide the company’s success, using her expertise to navigate market challenges. Her forward- thinking approach to integrating clean energy and reducing fossil fuel dependence  positions  the  company  for  long-term  profitability  and sustainability. Bintu earned a BSc in Public Administration from the University of Lagos.</p></div></div><div class="col-sm-6 col-lg-3"><div class="ag-member"><div class="ph"><img src="images/team/oluwatobi-asanre.jpeg" alt="Oluwatobi Asanre" style="object-position:top"></div><h3>Oluwatobi Asanre</h3><span> Head Of Internal Audit</span><p style="height: 270px;overflow: auto;">Oluwatobi Asanre is a seasoned Internal Audit professional with 12 years of experience in risk-based auditing, internal controls, corporate governance, and regulatory compliance across multiple industries, including manufacturing, engineering, retail, printing, and recycling.
<br>
He holds a B.Sc. in Accounting and an M.Sc. in Finance from Olabisi Onabanjo University and is an Associate Member of the Institute of Chartered Accountants of Nigeria (ICAN).
<br>
Currently serving as Head of Internal Audit at Arowolo Group of Companies, Lekki, Lagos, he provides strategic assurance and advisory services, strengthens internal control systems, assesses business risks, and promotes operational efficiency, financial integrity, and regulatory compliance to support organizational growth.</p></div></div><div class="col-sm-6 col-lg-3"><div class="ag-member"><div class="ph"><img src="images/team/augustine-alenu.jpeg" alt="Augustine Alenu" style="object-position:top"></div><h3>Augustine Alenu</h3><span>Business Head, Retail Downstream
</span>
<p style="height: 270px;overflow: auto;">
ALENU AUGUSTINE (M.Sc., MBA, B.Sc., FNIM, FCIA) is a seasoned business strategist and oil and gas professional with over 18 years of experience in financial management, business operations, and project management within the midstream and downstream oil and gas sectors. He holds an MBA in Financial Management and Strategy, an M.Sc. in Business Administration, and a B.Sc. (Hons) in Accounting. He has built an accomplished career with leading industry players, including Ascon Oil and Gas Limited and Masters Energy Oil and Gas Limited, where he held strategic positions and contributed to organizational growth and operational excellence. He currently serves as the *Business Head, Retail Downstream at Arowolo Oil and Gas Limited*, providing strategic leadership across retail operations, depot management, sales, marketing, and business development. His expertise spans financial planning and reporting, profitability improvement, operational controls, and the development and implementation of effective business strategies that enhance performance and strengthen market competitiveness. He has also participated in numerous local and international training programmes, conferences, and seminars, and has received performance awards in recognition of his contributions to the midstream and downstream oil and gas industry.   
</p>
</div></div><div class="col-sm-6 col-lg-3"><div class="ag-member"><div class="ph"><img src="images/team/soyemi-samson-ayodele.jpeg" alt="Soyemi Samson Ayodele" style="object-position:top"></div><h3>Soyemi Samson Ayodele</h3><span>Finance Manager</span><p style="height: 270px;overflow: auto;">Soyemi Samson Ayodele is an experienced finance professional with 12 years of career experience in financial management, budgeting, financial reporting, and financial control. As Finance Manager, he brings strong analytical skills and financial expertise to support strategic decision-making, ensure regulatory compliance, and promote effective resource management. He is an Associate Chartered Accountant (ACA), demonstrating his professional competence and commitment to financial excellence and accountability.</p></div></div><div class="col-sm-6 col-lg-3"><div class="ag-member"><div class="ph"><img src="images/team/chinwe-ofulue-banjo.jpeg" alt="Chinwe Ofulue Banjo" style="object-position:top"></div><h3>Chinwe Ofulue Banjo</h3><span>Head of Upstream Department</span><p style="height: 270px;overflow: auto;">Chinwe Ofulue Banjo is an accomplished oil and gas professional with 18 years of industry experience in the upstream and midstream sectors. As Head of the Upstream and Midstream Department, she brings extensive industry knowledge, strategic leadership, and a strong commitment to operational excellence, project coordination, and efficient resource management. Her professional expertise supports the effective delivery of energy projects, operational performance, and the achievement of organizational objectives.</p></div></div><div class="col-sm-6 col-lg-3"><div class="ag-member"><div class="ph"><img src="images/team/chikaodili-okeke.jpeg" alt="Chukwujekwu Chikaodili Okeke" style="object-position:top"></div><h3>Chukwujekwu Chikaodili Okeke</h3><span>Human Resources</span><p style="height: 270px;overflow: auto;">Chukwujekwu Chikaodili Okeke is a committed, results-oriented Human Resource professional with over six years' experience across banking, oil and gas, wholesale distribution and hospitality. She holds a BSc in Banking and Finance and a Diploma in Human Resource Management, and is a member of the Chartered Institute of Personnel Management (ACIPM) and the Chartered Institute of Bankers of Nigeria (CIBN). She designs strategic HR processes and policies that help employees and organizations achieve their goals, with a focus on building mutually beneficial relationships between the organization and its people.</p></div></div><div class="col-sm-6 col-lg-3"><div class="ag-member"><div class="ph"><img src="images/team/sulaimon-muizz-olalekan.jpeg" alt="Sulaimon Muizz Olalekan" style="object-position:top"></div><h3>Sulaimon Muizz Olalekan</h3><span>Finance Manager</span><p style="height: 270px;overflow: auto;">Accomplished Internal Auditor with over 7 years of progressive experience driving operational excellence and financial integrity across oil and gas, microfinance, and professional services sectors. Currently serving as Head of Internal Audit &amp; Control at Arowolo Oil and Gas, where he oversees comprehensive audit functions across 5 subsidiaries, reducing audit completion time while maintaining rigorous quality standards.<br><br>His expertise encompasses risk assessment, regulatory compliance, and internal control framework implementation, with a proven track record of identifying significant cost savings and operational inefficiencies. He has successfully improved loan portfolio quality by 25%, achieved 100% regulatory compliance rates, and saved organizations millions through targeted process improvements and fraud prevention measures.<br><br>As an Associate Chartered Accountant (ACA) with advanced proficiency in QuickBooks, Sage 50, and Power BI, he combines technical accounting knowledge with strategic audit methodologies. He is currently pursuing a Master's in Forensic Accounting and Auditing, bringing both practical experience and continuous professional development to deliver measurable audit outcomes that protect assets and enhance organizational performance.</p></div></div></div></div></section><section class="ag-cta"><div class="container d-flex flex-wrap justify-content-between align-items-center gap-3"><h2>Have a project or supply need? Talk to us.</h2><a class="ag-btn m-0" href="contact.html">Contact us</a></div></section></main><!-- Footer Start -->
